## Key Concepts
- Envelope encryption with per-tenant DEK
- KEK and DEK lifecycle in Azure Key Vault
- Zero-downtime KEK rotation using Durable Functions
- End-to-end tracing across Functions, Cosmos DB, and Data Lake
- Per-env CI/CD and access governance

## Code Example
```javascript
import { DefaultAzureCredential } from "@azure/identity";
import { KeyClient, CryptographyClient } from "@azure/keyvault-keys";

const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const keyClient = new KeyClient("https://<vault>.vault.azure.net", credential);
async function fetchTenantDEK(tenantId) {
  const key = await keyClient.getKey(`dek-${tenantId}`);
  // In practice, wrap/unwrap with a CryptographyClient here
  return key;
}
```

